---
import LegalLayout from "../components/LegalLayout.astro";
import Fact from "../components/Fact.astro";
import { COMPANY } from "../config/legal";

// Also the privacy policy Google's OAuth app verification reviews: the
// "Google user data" section must keep disclosing exactly which Google scopes
// are requested and how the data is used (see files/GOOGLE_OAUTH_VERIFICATION.md).
// Keep the scope list in sync with the scopes requested in apps/api/app.
// Retention: conversation_history_days in apps/api/app/core/plans.py only limits
// what the dashboard SHOWS -- nothing deletes old conversations yet (GDPR
// Phase 5), so this page must not promise automatic deletion.
const email = COMPANY.privacyEmail;
---

<LegalLayout
  doc="privacy"
  titleKey="PRIVACY"
  description="How Mielikkix AS collects, uses and protects personal data: legal bases, subprocessors, transfers, retention, your rights and Google user data."
>
  <Fragment slot="en">
    <section>
      <p>
        This policy explains what personal data Mielikkix collects, why, on what legal basis, who we share it with,
        how long we keep it and what rights you have. It covers the website mielikkix.ai, the dashboard
        app.mielikkix.ai, our API, the Mielikkix chat widget and our AI agents.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        The data controller is <strong>{COMPANY.legalName}</strong>, org. no. <Fact value={COMPANY.orgNumber} />,
        {" "}<Fact value={COMPANY.address} />, {COMPANY.country}. Contact for all privacy questions:
        {" "}<a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. Our two roles: controller and processor</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Controller</strong> for data about our own customers (businesses and their dashboard users), visitors
          to mielikkix.ai, people who request a demo, and people who chat with the Mielikkix chatbot on our own website.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Processor</strong> for data about our customers' own end users: people who chat with a customer's
          widget, call a customer's Voice Receptionist number or book through a customer's Booking Assistant. The
          business you contacted is the controller for that data and its privacy policy applies; we process it only on
          its instructions under our <a href="/dpa">Data Processing Agreement</a>. Please send requests about that data
          to the business. If you contact us, we will forward your request.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. What we collect, why, and our legal basis</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Data</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis (GDPR art. 6)</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Name, email, hashed password, business profile, uploaded FAQs/documents/products, plan</td>
              <td>Create and run your account and provide the service</td>
              <td>Contract (6(1)(b))</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Billing and invoicing records</td>
              <td>Accounting</td>
              <td>Legal obligation (6(1)(c)), Norwegian Bookkeeping Act</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Demo requests and contact messages (name, email, phone, company, message)</td>
              <td>Answer you and arrange a demo</td>
              <td>Steps before a contract (6(1)(b)) / legitimate interest (6(1)(f))</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Chats with the Mielikkix chatbot on mielikkix.ai, and any lead details you give it</td>
              <td>Answer your questions and follow up if you ask us to</td>
              <td>Legitimate interest (6(1)(f))</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Server and security logs (IP address, timestamps, request data)</td>
              <td>Security, abuse prevention, troubleshooting</td>
              <td>Legitimate interest (6(1)(f))</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Website usage statistics (Google Analytics)</td>
              <td>Understand how the website is used and improve it</td>
              <td>Consent (6(1)(a)), only if you click "Accept"</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Product-update emails</td>
              <td>Send news and tips</td>
              <td>Consent (6(1)(a)), withdraw any time via the unsubscribe link</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>End-user data processed for our customers (see section 2)</td>
              <td>Provide the chat, booking and voice services to the customer</td>
              <td>Determined by the customer as controller; we act under the DPA</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h3>End-user data we process for customers</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Chat messages sent to a business's chatbot, and the AI's replies, kept as conversation history for that business.</li>
        <li>Lead details a visitor submits (name, email, phone, message), shared with that business.</li>
        <li>Booking details (name, email, phone, requested appointment time) when a visitor books through Booking Assistant.</li>
        <li>
          For phone calls to a business's Voice Receptionist line: the call audio is transcribed to text by our telephony
          provider to carry on the conversation; call transcripts are held only in memory for the duration of the call
          today and are not currently written to a database.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. AI processing</h2>
      <p>
        Our products use large language models from external providers (see <a href="/subprocessors">Subprocessors</a>)
        to generate replies, classify support messages, draft review responses and analyse websites. The chatbot and
        voice assistant are AI systems, not people. They do not make decisions with legal or similarly significant
        effects about you (GDPR art. 22). We do not use customer or end-user data to train AI models, and our
        providers' API terms do not allow them to either <Fact value="{{VERIFY: confirm each provider's API data-use terms}}" />.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="google-calendar-data">
      <h2>5. Google user data (Google API Services)</h2>
      <h3>Google Calendar (Booking Assistant)</h3>
      <p>
        Booking Assistant lets a business connect their own Google Calendar so the assistant can check real
        availability and create real appointments on that business's behalf. This is entirely opt-in: a business only
        connects if they choose to use Booking Assistant, by signing in with their own Google account through Google's
        own consent screen.
      </p>
      <p>When a business connects their calendar, we request exactly two Google Calendar scopes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <code>calendar.freebusy</code> -- read-only access to when the connected calendar is busy or free. We never read
          the contents, titles, descriptions, or attendees of a business's existing calendar events -- only whether a
          given time slot is already taken.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>calendar.events</code> -- lets Mielikkix create new calendar events representing appointments booked
          through the assistant, with the visitor who booked as an attendee (so Google emails them a calendar invite
          directly). We do not read, modify, or delete events we did not create.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We also request basic account email (<code>userinfo.email</code>) solely so the business's own dashboard can
        show them which Google account is connected (e.g. "Connected as: owner@theirbusiness.com").
      </p>
      <h3>Google Business Profile (Review &amp; Reputation)</h3>
      <p>
        With <code>business.manage</code>, a business that connects its Google Business Profile lets us read the
        reviews on its own locations and publish the replies that the business has approved. We don't change anything
        else on the profile.
      </p>
      <h3>Google Analytics and Search Console (SEO Audit)</h3>
      <p>
        With the read-only scopes <code>analytics.readonly</code> and <code>webmasters.readonly</code>, a business that
        connects them lets us read its own website traffic and search-performance figures to prioritise its SEO audit.
        We never change its Analytics or Search Console settings.
      </p>
      <h3>How Google user data is stored and used</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>How this data is stored:</strong> the OAuth refresh token Google issues is encrypted at rest before it
        is ever written to our database, using a symmetric key held only on our own servers. It is decrypted only in
        memory, immediately before making an API call on that business's behalf, and is never logged, emailed, or
        exposed to any other business.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>How this data is used:</strong> solely to provide the feature the business connected it for (checking
        availability and creating bookings, handling its reviews, or its SEO audit). We do not use Google user data for
        advertising, do not sell it, do not share it with any third party except the Google API itself and the business
        that owns the connection, and do not use it to train any AI model.
      </p>
      <p>
        A business can disconnect any Google integration at any time from its own Settings page, which deletes the
        stored refresh token immediately. Disconnecting Calendar does not delete already-created calendar events (those
        are removed the normal way, directly in Google Calendar).
      </p>
      <p>
        Mielikkix's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
        {" "}<a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
        including the Limited Use requirements.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. Who we share data with</h2>
      <p>
        We use carefully chosen service providers (subprocessors), each receiving only what it needs for its task. The
        full, current list, with purpose and location, is on our <a href="/subprocessors">Subprocessors</a> page. We do
        not sell personal data. We may also disclose data if the law requires it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. Transfers outside the EEA</h2>
      <p>
        Several providers (for example Groq, OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Twilio and Resend) are based in the USA. When
        personal data is transferred there, we rely on the EU-US Data Privacy Framework where the provider is
        certified, or on the EU Standard Contractual Clauses <Fact value="{{VERIFY: mechanism per vendor}}" />. You can ask
        us for a copy of the relevant safeguards.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>8. How long we keep data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Account data:</strong> while your account is active; deleted within <Fact value="{{VERIFY: 30}}" /> days after you close it, except what we must keep by law.</li>
        <li><strong>Accounting records:</strong> 5 years after the end of the financial year (Norwegian Bookkeeping Act).</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Conversation history and leads (processed for customers):</strong> kept while the business's account is
          active, or until the business deletes it or asks us to. When the account is closed, it is deleted along with
          the account. Your plan decides how much history you can see in the dashboard. Automatic deletion after a set
          retention period is on the way <Fact value="{{VERIFY: max retention period}}" />.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Voice calls:</strong> transcripts are only held in memory during the call and are not stored.</li>
        <li><strong>Demo requests:</strong> <Fact value="{{VERIFY: 12 months}}" /> after our last contact, unless you become a customer.</li>
        <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> <Fact value="{{VERIFY: log retention}}" />.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Analytics data:</strong> <Fact value="{{VERIFY: GA4 data retention setting, 2 or 14 months}}" />.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>9. Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        mielikkix.ai only uses necessary storage unless you accept analytics in our cookie banner. Google Analytics
        loads only after you accept, and you can change your choice any time under "Cookie settings" in the footer. Fonts
        are served from our own server. See the <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a> for every cookie and storage key.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>10. Security</h2>
      <p>
        Passwords are hashed, never stored in plain text. OAuth refresh tokens are encrypted at rest. Traffic is
        encrypted with TLS. Dashboard sessions use httpOnly cookies. Each business can only access its own data. More on
        our <a href="/security">Security</a> page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>11. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the GDPR and the Norwegian Personal Data Act you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>access the personal data we hold about you;</li>
        <li>have inaccurate data corrected;</li>
        <li>have your data erased ("right to be forgotten");</li>
        <li>restrict processing;</li>
        <li>data portability (receive your data in a machine-readable format);</li>
        <li>object to processing based on legitimate interest;</li>
        <li>withdraw consent at any time, without affecting processing that took place before.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> to use any of these rights. We answer within one month, and may ask
        you to verify your identity first. Account holders can currently close their account by emailing us; self-service
        export and deletion in the dashboard are coming.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can complain to the Norwegian Data Protection Authority,
        {" "}<a href="https://www.datatilsynet.no" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Datatilsynet</a>. In the UK you can
        complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Information Commissioner's Office (ICO)</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>12. Children</h2>
      <p>Our services are for businesses and not directed at children. Account holders must be 18 or older.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>13. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We will update this policy when our services or the law change. The date and version at the top show the current
        version. If a change is material, we will tell account holders by email or in the dashboard.
      </p>
    </section>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="no">
    <section>
      <p>
        Denne erklæringen forklarer hvilke personopplysninger Mielikkix samler inn, hvorfor, på hvilket rettslig
        grunnlag, hvem vi deler dem med, hvor lenge vi lagrer dem og hvilke rettigheter du har. Den gjelder nettstedet
        mielikkix.ai, dashbordet app.mielikkix.ai, API-et vårt, Mielikkix-chatwidgeten og AI-agentene våre.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>1. Hvem vi er</h2>
      <p>
        Behandlingsansvarlig er <strong>{COMPANY.legalName}</strong>, org.nr. <Fact value={COMPANY.orgNumber} />,
        {" "}<Fact value={COMPANY.address} />, Norge. Kontakt for alle personvernspørsmål:
        {" "}<a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. Våre to roller: behandlingsansvarlig og databehandler</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Behandlingsansvarlig</strong> for opplysninger om våre egne kunder (bedrifter og deres dashbordbrukere),
          besøkende på mielikkix.ai, personer som ber om en demo, og personer som chatter med Mielikkix-chatboten på vårt
          eget nettsted.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Databehandler</strong> for opplysninger om kundenes egne sluttbrukere: personer som chatter med en kundes
          widget, ringer en kundes Voice Receptionist-nummer eller booker via en kundes Booking Assistant. Bedriften du
          kontaktet er behandlingsansvarlig for disse opplysningene, og bedriftens personvernerklæring gjelder. Vi
          behandler dem bare etter bedriftens instrukser i henhold til vår <a href="/dpa">databehandleravtale</a>.
          Send henvendelser om slike opplysninger til bedriften. Kontakter du oss, videresender vi henvendelsen.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. Hva vi samler inn, hvorfor og rettslig grunnlag</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Opplysninger</th><th>Formål</th><th>Rettslig grunnlag (GDPR art. 6)</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Navn, e-post, hashet passord, bedriftsprofil, opplastede FAQ-er/dokumenter/produkter, abonnement</td>
              <td>Opprette og drifte kontoen din og levere tjenesten</td>
              <td>Avtale (6(1)(b))</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Fakturerings- og regnskapsopplysninger</td>
              <td>Regnskap</td>
              <td>Rettslig forpliktelse (6(1)(c)), bokføringsloven</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Demoforespørsler og henvendelser (navn, e-post, telefon, bedrift, melding)</td>
              <td>Svare deg og avtale en demo</td>
              <td>Tiltak før avtaleinngåelse (6(1)(b)) / berettiget interesse (6(1)(f))</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Samtaler med Mielikkix-chatboten på mielikkix.ai, og kontaktopplysninger du oppgir der</td>
              <td>Svare på spørsmålene dine og følge opp hvis du ber om det</td>
              <td>Berettiget interesse (6(1)(f))</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Server- og sikkerhetslogger (IP-adresse, tidspunkter, forespørselsdata)</td>
              <td>Sikkerhet, forebygging av misbruk, feilsøking</td>
              <td>Berettiget interesse (6(1)(f))</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Bruksstatistikk for nettstedet (Google Analytics)</td>
              <td>Forstå hvordan nettstedet brukes og forbedre det</td>
              <td>Samtykke (6(1)(a)), bare hvis du klikker «Godta»</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>E-post med produktnyheter</td>
              <td>Sende nyheter og tips</td>
              <td>Samtykke (6(1)(a)), kan trekkes tilbake når som helst via avmeldingslenken</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Sluttbrukeropplysninger vi behandler for kunder (se punkt 2)</td>
              <td>Levere chat-, booking- og taletjenestene til kunden</td>
              <td>Fastsettes av kunden som behandlingsansvarlig; vi handler etter databehandleravtalen</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h3>Sluttbrukeropplysninger vi behandler for kunder</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Chatmeldinger sendt til en bedrifts chatbot, og AI-ens svar, lagret som samtalehistorikk for bedriften.</li>
        <li>Kontaktopplysninger en besøkende sender inn (navn, e-post, telefon, melding), som deles med bedriften.</li>
        <li>Bookingopplysninger (navn, e-post, telefon, ønsket tidspunkt) når en besøkende booker via Booking Assistant.</li>
        <li>
          For telefonsamtaler til en bedrifts Voice Receptionist-linje: samtalelyden gjøres om til tekst av vår
          telefonileverandør for å føre samtalen; transkripsjonen holdes kun i minnet mens samtalen pågår og lagres i dag
          ikke i en database.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. AI-behandling</h2>
      <p>
        Produktene våre bruker store språkmodeller fra eksterne leverandører (se <a href="/subprocessors">Underleverandører</a>)
        for å lage svar, klassifisere supporthenvendelser, lage utkast til svar på anmeldelser og analysere nettsteder.
        Chatboten og taleassistenten er AI-systemer, ikke mennesker. De tar ikke avgjørelser som har rettsvirkning eller
        tilsvarende betydelig virkning for deg (GDPR art. 22). Vi bruker ikke kunde- eller sluttbrukerdata til å trene
        AI-modeller, og leverandørenes API-vilkår tillater heller ikke dem å gjøre det <Fact value="{{VERIFY: bekreft hver leverandørs API-vilkår for databruk}}" />.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. Opplysninger fra Google (Google API Services)</h2>
      <h3>Google Kalender (Booking Assistant)</h3>
      <p>
        Booking Assistant lar en bedrift koble til sin egen Google Kalender slik at assistenten kan sjekke reell
        tilgjengelighet og opprette avtaler på vegne av bedriften. Dette er helt frivillig: en bedrift kobler bare til hvis
        den velger å bruke Booking Assistant, ved å logge inn med sin egen Google-konto via Googles eget samtykkebilde.
      </p>
      <p>Når en bedrift kobler til kalenderen, ber vi om nøyaktig to Google Kalender-tilganger:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <code>calendar.freebusy</code> – kun lesetilgang til når kalenderen er opptatt eller ledig. Vi leser aldri innhold,
          titler, beskrivelser eller deltakere i bedriftens eksisterende avtaler, bare om et tidspunkt allerede er opptatt.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>calendar.events</code> – lar Mielikkix opprette nye kalenderavtaler for bookinger gjort via assistenten, med
          den besøkende som deltaker (slik at Google sender dem en kalenderinvitasjon direkte). Vi leser, endrer eller
          sletter ikke avtaler vi ikke har opprettet selv.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Vi ber også om kontoens e-postadresse (<code>userinfo.email</code>) kun for å vise bedriften hvilken Google-konto
        som er tilkoblet i dashbordet.
      </p>
      <h3>Google Bedriftsprofil (Review &amp; Reputation)</h3>
      <p>
        Med <code>business.manage</code> lar en bedrift som kobler til sin Google Bedriftsprofil oss lese anmeldelsene på
        egne lokasjoner og publisere svar som bedriften har godkjent. Vi endrer ikke noe annet på profilen.
      </p>
      <h3>Google Analytics og Search Console (SEO-revisjon)</h3>
      <p>
        Med lesetilgangene <code>analytics.readonly</code> og <code>webmasters.readonly</code> lar en bedrift som kobler
        dem til oss lese nettstedets egen trafikk og søkeytelse for å prioritere SEO-revisjonen. Vi endrer aldri
        innstillinger i Analytics eller Search Console.
      </p>
      <h3>Lagring og bruk av opplysninger fra Google</h3>
      <p>
        OAuth-tokenet Google utsteder krypteres før det lagres i databasen, med en nøkkel som bare finnes på våre egne
        servere. Det dekrypteres kun i minnet rett før et API-kall på bedriftens vegne, og blir aldri logget, sendt på
        e-post eller vist til andre bedrifter.
      </p>
      <p>
        Opplysningene brukes kun til funksjonen bedriften koblet dem til for (tilgjengelighet og booking, anmeldelser
        eller SEO-revisjon). Vi bruker dem ikke til reklame, selger dem ikke, deler dem ikke med andre enn Googles eget
        API og bedriften som eier tilkoblingen, og bruker dem ikke til å trene AI-modeller.
      </p>
      <p>
        En bedrift kan når som helst koble fra en Google-integrasjon under Innstillinger, og da slettes det lagrede
        tokenet umiddelbart. Å koble fra kalenderen sletter ikke avtaler som allerede er opprettet.
      </p>
      <p>
        Mielikkix sin bruk og overføring av informasjon mottatt fra Google API-er følger
        {" "}<a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
        inkludert kravene om begrenset bruk (Limited Use).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. Hvem vi deler opplysninger med</h2>
      <p>
        Vi bruker nøye utvalgte tjenesteleverandører (underleverandører), som hver bare får det de trenger for sin
        oppgave. Den fullstendige, oppdaterte listen med formål og plassering finner du under
        {" "}<a href="/subprocessors">Underleverandører</a>. Vi selger ikke personopplysninger. Vi kan også utlevere
        opplysninger når loven krever det.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. Overføring ut av EØS</h2>
      <p>
        Flere leverandører (for eksempel Groq, OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Twilio og Resend) holder til i USA. Ved
        overføring dit bygger vi på EU–US Data Privacy Framework der leverandøren er sertifisert, ellers på EUs
        standardkontraktsbestemmelser <Fact value="{{VERIFY: overføringsgrunnlag per leverandør}}" />. Du kan be oss om en
        kopi av garantiene.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>8. Hvor lenge vi lagrer opplysninger</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Kontoopplysninger:</strong> så lenge kontoen er aktiv; slettes innen <Fact value="{{VERIFY: 30}}" /> dager etter at du avslutter den, unntatt det loven krever at vi beholder.</li>
        <li><strong>Regnskapsmateriale:</strong> 5 år etter regnskapsårets slutt (bokføringsloven).</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Samtalehistorikk og leads (behandlet for kunder):</strong> lagres mens bedriftens konto er aktiv, eller
          til bedriften sletter dem eller ber oss om det. Når kontoen avsluttes, slettes de sammen med den. Abonnementet
          avgjør hvor mye historikk som vises i dashbordet. Automatisk sletting etter en fast lagringsperiode er på vei
          {" "}<Fact value="{{VERIFY: maks lagringstid}}" />.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Telefonsamtaler:</strong> transkripsjoner holdes kun i minnet under samtalen og lagres ikke.</li>
